function getHelpTopicsV5102() {
  return [
      {id:'start',title:'Start Here: Admin Workflow',nav:'dashboard',html:'<p>The Admin Portal is the working space for building, reviewing, customizing, optimizing, publishing, and auditing schedules. Staff see only the Staff Portal snapshot that you publish.</p><h4>Start here</h4><ol><li><b>Check data readiness:</b> review Staff Manager, Student Manager, Bell Schedule Manager, Campus Manager, and Data Manager when source information has changed.</li><li><b>Check attendance:</b> review Attendance Manager and the Dashboard before generating a schedule.</li><li><b>Generate or customize:</b> use Generate Schedules for the normal schedule, Scenario Preview for future or hypothetical days, or Customize Schedule for manual edits.</li><li><b>Review outputs:</b> check Staff Schedules, Student Schedules, Break Schedule, Dashboard alerts, and Logic Review.</li><li><b>Publish:</b> publish only after the working schedule is ready for staff to see.</li></ol><h4>When to use each path</h4><ul><li><b>Generate Schedules:</b> normal daily schedule rebuild.</li><li><b>Scenario Preview:</b> future date, projected absences, or alternate day testing.</li><li><b>Customize Schedule:</b> manual override when the generator needs human judgment.</li><li><b>Optimize Schedule:</b> simulation when coverage gaps remain.</li><li><b>Historical Schedules:</b> restore, republish, favorite, lock, or review previous snapshots.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout"><b>Best practice:</b> Refresh Data, generate or customize, review warnings, then publish. Working admin changes are not staff-facing until the right publish action runs.</div><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="dashboard">Dashboard</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="generate">Generate</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="custom">Customize</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="publish">Publish</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="logic">Logic Review</button></div>'},
      {id:'dashboard',title:'Dashboard',nav:'dashboard',html:'<p>The Dashboard is the home base for the portal. It gives a quick view of schedule readiness, attendance impacts, data quality, publish status, and items that may need action before staff use the schedule.</p><h4>Top actions</h4><ul><li><b>Refresh Data</b> reloads portal data from the spreadsheet and server-side model.</li><li><b>Generate Schedules</b> rebuilds assignments, break/lunch recommendations, and dashboard outputs from the current source data.</li><li><b>Publish</b> sends the current working schedule to the Staff Portal and saves a historical snapshot.</li><li><b>Search</b> finds students, staff, rooms, and related schedule information across the portal.</li></ul><h4>Status pills</h4><ul><li><b>Optimization Active</b> means the current working schedule was generated with temporary optimization rules.</li><li><b>Customization Active</b> means a custom schedule has been published and remains active. Click the × to clear the custom state, regenerate the normal schedule, and leave that normal schedule unpublished for review.</li><li><b>Unpublished Schedule</b> means the working schedule differs from the staff-facing published schedule. Click the × on the pill to cancel the unpublished version and return the admin schedule views to the last published schedule.</li></ul><h4>Dashboard tiles</h4><ul><li><b>To Do</b> is for user-generated follow-up items. Use it to capture reminders, notes, and action prompts that help administrators track what still needs attention.</li><li><b>Today / schedule summary</b> summarizes what the current generated schedule is based on, including the active schedule type and key schedule counts.</li><li><b>Attendance tile</b> show staff or student absences that may affect coverage. Use Attendance Manager for the full record.</li><li><b>Unassigned or coverage-risk tiles</b> point to students, periods, rooms, or support needs that the generator could not fully place.</li><li><b>Publish/status tiles</b> help confirm whether staff are seeing the same schedule that administrators are reviewing.</li></ul><h4>Tile controls</h4><ul><li>Some tiles can be collapsed to make the dashboard more compact.</li><li>Dashboard tiles may be moved or resized depending on the current layout tools in the script.</li><li>Use the dashboard as a triage screen first, then open the matching manager or schedule page for details.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout">Best practice: after changing staff, students, attendance, bell schedule, campus rules, or settings, refresh data, generate schedules, review dashboard alerts, then publish only when the schedule is ready.</div><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="start">Start Here</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="settings">Settings</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="generate">Generate</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="publish">Publish</button></div>'},
      {id:'staffManager',title:'Staff Manager',nav:'staff',html:'<p>Staff Manager controls who can be scheduled, when they are available, which students or rooms they should not cover, and any special priority holds that affect assignment and break/lunch planning.</p><h4>Main staff fields</h4><ul><li><b>Name</b> is the staff member name used across schedules, student assignments, attendance, and the Staff Portal.</li><li><b>Absent Today</b> temporarily removes the staff member from same-day generated coverage.</li><li><b>Status</b> controls whether the staff member is eligible for scheduling. Active staff are schedulable; non-active status values are retained for records but should not be treated as normal coverage.</li><li><b>Interested in Overtime</b> is used only when emergency lunch coverage is allowed in Settings and the scheduler needs additional coverage options.</li><li><b>Support Type</b> identifies the staff role for soft matching. Behavior needs prefer Behavior Interventionists; Instruction needs prefer Special Education Assistants. Cross-coverage is controlled in Settings.</li><li><b>Total Absences</b> is informational and can help administrators review attendance patterns.</li></ul><h4>Staff status levels</h4><ul><li><b>Active</b> means the staff member can be considered for assignments if all other rules allow it.</li><li><b>Inactive, Leave, Substitute, or other non-active statuses</b> keep the staff profile available but should prevent the person from being used like regular active coverage.</li><li><b>Absent Today</b> is separate from status. A staff member can still be Active overall but unavailable today because they are marked absent.</li></ul><h4>Blocked Times</h4><p>Blocked Times are periods or clock-time ranges when the staff member should not be scheduled. You can enter more than one block separated by slashes, commas, or new lines.</p><ul><li><code>Period 2</code> blocks the staff member during that schedule item.</li><li><code>Lunch</code> blocks the staff member during lunch.</li><li><code>9:15 AM - 10:00 AM</code> blocks a clock-time range.</li><li><code>&gt; 1:30 PM</code> blocks after a time.</li><li><code>&lt; 10:00 AM</code> blocks before a time.</li><li><code>Period 3 [Wednesday]</code> limits the block to that day when day-qualified rules are being evaluated.</li></ul><h4>Priority Holds</h4><ul><li>Priority Hold period names follow Bell Schedule display names where available, while the internal period key remains stable.</li><li>Locations include campus rooms and off-campus sites.</li><li><b>Coach</b> is a special hold. It protects that staff member from generated 15-minute breaks and 30-minute lunches, so the break/lunch builder does not treat them as someone who should receive a normal break/lunch assignment.</li><li><b>Period @ Room holds</b>, such as <code>Period 2 @ Room 101</code>, reserve the staff member for a specific period/location combination when the scheduler is making priority decisions.</li><li>Priority holds do not replace blocked times. Use blocked times for unavailable time; use priority holds for intentional scheduling preference or protection.</li></ul><h4>Lunch/Break Preferences</h4><ul><li>Rest preferences rank otherwise legal lunch/break windows; they do not make a staff member unavailable like Blocked Times do.</li><li><b>Prefer this time</b> favors the selected timing but allows another legal time when needed.</li><li><b>Require this time</b> only schedules in the selected timing. If no legal matching window exists, the rest item is left unscheduled for review.</li><li><b>Specific period/item</b> can use a bell-schedule label such as <code>Period 6</code>, <code>Lunch</code>, or <code>Break</code>.</li><li><b>Specific time window</b> can use a range such as <code>1:30 PM - 2:00 PM</code>.</li></ul><h4>Blocked Students and Blocked Rooms</h4><ul><li><b>Blocked Students</b> prevents this staff member from being assigned to selected students.</li><li><b>Blocked Rooms</b> prevents this staff member from being assigned in selected rooms/locations, including off-campus sites.</li><li>Student Manager also has blocked-staff rules. If either side blocks the pairing, the scheduler should treat that staff/student combination as unavailable.</li></ul><h4>Staff Assignment</h4><p><b>Staff Assignment</b> shows where the selected staff member is currently listed as primary or secondary support by schedule item. Use the editor when you need to directly adjust staff-to-student relationships from the staff profile side.</p><h4>Staff list tools</h4><ul><li>Use search to find a staff profile quickly.</li><li>Drag staff names to adjust staff order/ranking, then save the order.</li><li>Use Show Alerts to display or hide manager badges such as absent, inactive, blocked, priority holds, lunch/break preferences, and rest-preference requirements.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout">Best practice: use Active/Absent/Blocked Times for hard availability, Blocked Students/Rooms for hard assignment restrictions, Priority Holds for intentional protection, and Lunch/Break Preferences for rest timing without blocking assignments.</div><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="studentManager">Student Manager</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="logic">Scheduling Logic</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="breaks">Break/Lunch</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="attendance">Attendance</button></div>'},
      {id:'studentManager',title:'Student Manager',nav:'students',html:'<p>Student Manager controls student support needs, schedule items, locations, pairing restrictions, and secondary-as-primary day overrides used by the scheduling engine.</p><h4>Core student fields</h4><ul><li><b>Student name</b> is used across student schedules, staff schedules, customization, and reports.</li><li><b>Schedule item / period</b> identifies when the support need occurs.</li><li><b>Location / room</b> tells the scheduler where support should happen.</li><li><b>Degree of Support</b> identifies the level or style of support needed, such as individual support or group-compatible support.</li><li><b>Support Type</b> identifies whether the need is Behavior, Instruction, or N/A so the scheduler can prefer the best-matched staff type.</li><li><b>Notes or links</b> provide review context for administrators.</li></ul><h4>Support rules</h4><ul><li>Required support should be assigned before optional or lower-risk needs.</li><li>Individual support is more restrictive than group support.</li><li>Group support can combine students only when period, location, capacity, and compatibility rules allow it.</li><li>If no support is needed, the student should show as not requiring coverage rather than unassigned.</li></ul><h4>Blocked staff</h4><ul><li><b>Blocked Staff</b> prevents selected staff from being assigned to that student.</li><li>If the staff profile also blocks the student, either side blocks the pairing.</li><li>Blocked pairings are treated as hard restrictions and should not be overridden by priority order.</li></ul><h4>Alternative Student-Level Staff Rank Order</h4><ul><li>Student Manager can store an optional fallback staff order for an individual student.</li><li>The two-column picker shows active staff on the left and the selected rank order on the right.</li><li>The scheduler still uses Priority Holds and same-period Primary/Secondary first.</li><li>If the student-level order is set, that list is tried before familiar staff/general staff rank order. Unlisted active staff remain available afterward as a last resort.</li></ul><h4>Dynamic periods and day overrides</h4><ul><li>Bell Schedule Manager controls the live list of schedule items, including renamed periods and added period blocks.</li><li>Additional periods appear in Student Manager so each student can receive location, support, primary staff, and secondary staff values.</li><li><b>Use Secondary as Primary</b> swaps the student primary/secondary preference on selected weekdays during generation. Example: if Wednesday is checked, Wednesday scheduling treats Secondary as Primary and Primary as Secondary for that student.</li><li>Assignment Analyzer and generated outputs should show the display period name while preserving the internal period key for logic.</li></ul><h4>Off-campus locations</h4><ul><li>Off-campus sites created in Campus Manager appear in student location dropdowns.</li><li>When a student is off campus, the assigned staff member is not treated as available for main-campus break/lunch coverage during the off-campus window plus buffer.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="staffManager">Staff Manager</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="dataManager">Data Manager</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="logic">Scheduling Logic</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="generate">Generate</button></div>'},
      {id:'dataManager',title:'Data Manager',nav:'dataManager',html:'<p>Data Manager provides links and review tools for the source data that feeds scheduling. Use it when a generated schedule does not match what you expected.</p><ul><li><b>Source links</b> open the underlying sheets or related data views.</li><li>Review staff, student, room, calendar, and schedule data here before assuming the generator made a logic error.</li><li>After changing source data, refresh data before generating again.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout">Best practice: confirm the source data, refresh the portal, then regenerate.</div><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="studentManager">Student Manager</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="generate">Generate</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="settings">Settings</button></div>'},
      {id:'calendarManager',title:'Calendar Manager',nav:'calendar',html:'<p>Calendar Manager maps dates to schedule types and stores Special Events. Special Events can override normal student schedule needs during the event window, assign selected staff, and sync the event name into that date calendar note. Scenario Preview, auto-publish, dashboard context, and daily schedule selection rely on this mapping.</p><ul><li>Assign schedule types to specific dates.</li><li>Represent minimum days, alternate schedules, holidays, and non-student days when they affect scheduling.</li><li>If the portal uses the wrong schedule for a date, check Calendar Manager first.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="bellSchedule">Bell Schedule</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="scenario">Scenario Preview</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="generate">Generate</button></div>'},
      {id:'bellSchedule',title:'Bell Schedule Manager',nav:'schedule',html:'<p>Bell Schedule Manager defines schedule types and includes a setup area for period display names/additional blocks. Core Break and Lunch stay fixed, and added blocks can be classified as Instruction, Break, or Lunch.</p><ul><li><b>Schedule type</b> separates Regular Day, Minimum Day, alternate-day schedules, and other patterns.</li><li><b>Period/item labels</b> should match labels used in blocked times and student schedule data.</li><li><b>Start and end times</b> support time-based blocking, break/lunch planning, and schedule display.</li><li><b>Lunch or special items</b> should be included if they need to be scheduled, blocked, or displayed.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="calendarManager">Calendar</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="campusManager">Campus</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="generate">Generate</button></div>'},
      {id:'campusManager',title:'Campus Manager',nav:'campus',html:'<p>Campus Manager stores location and campus rule information used by the scheduler.</p><ul><li><b>Rooms and locations</b> help determine where students and staff can be assigned.</li><li><b>Structured or capacity-limited rooms</b> can affect whether students can be grouped.</li><li><b>Campus workday settings</b> may be used for attendance and partial-day calculations.</li><li><b>Blocked rooms</b> in staff profiles prevent assignments in those locations.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="bellSchedule">Bell Schedule</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="studentManager">Student Manager</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="logic">Scheduling Logic</button></div>'},
      {id:'generate',title:'Generate Schedules',nav:'dashboard',html:'<p><b>Generate Schedules</b> runs the scheduling engine using active staff, student support needs, bell schedule, attendance, campus rules, and Settings.</p><ol><li>Refresh data after changing source records.</li><li>Click Generate Schedules.</li><li>Review Dashboard alerts, Staff Schedule, Student Schedule, Break Schedule, and Logic Review.</li><li>Use Optimize Schedule when unresolved coverage gaps need simulation.</li><li>Use Customize Schedule when a human override is needed.</li><li>Publish when the working schedule is ready for staff.</li></ol><div class="helpCallout"><b>What this does:</b> replaces the working generated schedule. <b>What this does not do:</b> it does not automatically publish to staff unless a publish or auto-publish action runs.</div><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="start">Start Here</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="dashboard">Dashboard</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="logic">Logic Review</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="optimize">Optimize</button></div>'},
      {id:'publish',title:'Publishing and Staff Portal',nav:'staffSchedules',html:'<p>Publishing writes the current Staff, Student, and Break schedule views to the Staff Portal and saves a Historical Schedule snapshot.</p><ul><li>Regular generated schedules require publishing before staff see them.</li><li>Custom schedules publish immediately when you click Publish Custom Schedule.</li><li>Scenario schedules can be saved as a draft snapshot or published for future/current use.</li><li>If staff do not see a recent change, check the publish status tile and republish the intended schedule.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout">Publish is the handoff from admin review to staff-facing schedule access.</div><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="staffportal">Staff Portal</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="history">Historical</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="regular">Regular Schedule</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="settings">Settings</button></div>'},
      {id:'scenario',title:'Scenario Preview',nav:'scenario',html:'<p>Scenario Preview is used to test a future or alternate day without changing source data.</p><ol><li>Select a date.</li><li>Confirm or override the schedule type.</li><li>Use Project Potential Absences for hypothetical staff or student absences.</li><li>Click Run Preview.</li><li>Review Summary, Staff Schedule, Student Schedule, and Break Schedule.</li><li>Use Save Schedule to store a draft snapshot or Publish Scenario to make it upcoming/current.</li></ol><p>Known absences come from Attendance. Projected absences are scenario-only and do not write to Attendance.</p><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="attendance">Attendance</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="history">Historical</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="publish">Publishing</button></div>'},
      {id:'custom',title:'Customize Schedule',nav:'customBuilder',html:'<p>Customize Schedule lets you drag student coverage pills between staff/period cells. It allows rule violations, but warnings are shown.</p><ol><li>Load the current schedule or open a historical snapshot with the pencil icon.</li><li>Drag pills to adjust student coverage.</li><li>Review warnings such as group max or different locations.</li><li>Click Lock Coverage & Build Breaks to generate break/lunch recommendations from the customized coverage map.</li><li>Edit break/lunch rows as needed.</li><li>Click Publish Custom Schedule.</li></ol><div class="helpCallout">Custom schedules publish immediately and show Customization Active. Clicking the × on the Customization Active pill clears the custom state, regenerates a normal schedule, and leaves the normal schedule unpublished until you choose to publish it.</div><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="breaks">Break/Lunch</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="history">Historical</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="publish">Publishing</button></div>'},
      {id:'breaks',title:'Break/Lunch Builder',nav:'customBuilder',html:'<p>The Break/Lunch Builder uses the locked customized coverage grid as its source of truth.</p><h4>How it should work</h4><ul><li>Build recommendations using the same scheduling priorities where possible.</li><li>Use free time before interrupting student coverage.</li><li>Schedule 30-minute lunches before 15-minute breaks when generating normal rest schedules.</li><li>Rank lunch/break timing middle-out from the target block, avoid the first 90 minutes when legal alternatives exist, and apply staff rest preferences after hard rules.</li><li>Show whether coverage is needed.</li><li>Filter covering staff to available staff, while allowing lead staff as manual coverage options.</li><li>Warn for duplicate break/lunch types for the same staff member.</li></ul><h4>Rest preference strength</h4><ul><li><b>Prefer this time</b> favors the preferred timing but can fall back to another legal time.</li><li><b>Require this time</b> only schedules in the preferred timing; otherwise the rest item is left unscheduled for review.</li></ul><p><b>Recheck Coverage</b> audits the current rows. It should not rebuild or overwrite manual edits.</p><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="custom">Customize</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="staffManager">Staff Manager</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="logic">Scheduling Logic</button></div>'},
      {id:'optimize',title:'Optimize Schedule',nav:'scheduleOptimizer',html:'<p>Optimize Schedule runs temporary rule-relaxing simulations when students remain uncovered. It can expand group caps, temporarily group selected individual students, or explicitly allow selected students to remain unstaffed.</p><ol><li>Open Optimize Schedule.</li><li>Run Assignment Optimization Simulation.</li><li>Review options.</li><li>Apply & Generate only if you want that optimized schedule to become the working schedule.</li></ol><div class="helpCallout"><b>Current scope:</b> Optimize Schedule now has modes for student support coverage, lunch/break coverage, or both. Rest Optimization suggests safe preference relaxations such as changing a required rest preference to Prefer this time; it does not silently change preferences unless you apply an option.</div><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="generate">Generate</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="logic">Logic Review</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="settings">Settings</button></div>'},
      {id:'history',title:'Historical Schedules',nav:'history',html:'<p>Historical Schedules stores published, saved, scenario, custom, optimized, and regular schedule snapshots.</p><h4>Actions</h4><ul><li><b>View</b> opens the read-only snapshot.</li><li><b>Publish</b> republishes that historical schedule.</li><li><b>Pencil</b> opens the snapshot in Customize Schedule.</li><li><b>Star</b> favorites the snapshot.</li><li><b>Lock</b> marks it as a regular schedule.</li><li><b>Save Notes</b> stores your notes.</li><li><b>Trash</b> deletes the snapshot.</li></ul><p>Multiple locked schedules can be used as regular schedule options.</p><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="regular">Regular Schedule</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="custom">Customize</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="publish">Publishing</button></div>'},
      {id:'regular',title:'Regular Schedule',nav:'regularSchedule',html:'<p>Regular Schedule shows historical schedules marked with the lock icon. If Display Regular Schedule on Staff Portal is enabled, staff can access these schedules as reference schedules.</p><p>The pill label comes from the schedule note before the slash. Example: <b>123 XYZ / notes here</b> displays as <b>123 XYZ</b>.</p><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="history">Historical</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="staffportal">Staff Portal</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="settings">Settings</button></div>'},
      {id:'attendance',title:'Attendance Manager',nav:'attendanceManager',html:'<p>Attendance Manager shows monthly staff attendance and individual attendance history.</p><ol><li>Select a month.</li><li>Review full-day absences marked A.</li><li>Review partial-day missed hours as negative numbers.</li><li>Click a staff name to open their individual attendance history.</li><li>Add, edit, delete, or print records as needed.</li></ol><p>Partial-day hours use the campus workday start/end time.</p><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="staffManager">Staff Manager</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="scenario">Scenario Preview</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="settings">Settings</button></div>'},
      {id:'staffportal',title:'Staff Portal',nav:'settings',html:'<p>The Staff Portal is the staff-facing view of the published schedule. Admins open it from the gray <b>Staff Portal</b> shortcut in the lower menu after a Staff Portal base URL is configured in System Admin.</p><ul><li>The shortcut opens the Staff Portal in a separate browser tab/window.</li><li>Staff see the published staff-facing schedule, not every unsaved admin change.</li><li>Regular Schedule access depends on locked historical schedules and the related Staff Portal display setting.</li><li>Staff absence reports write to Attendance and can trigger email notifications configured in Settings.</li><li>If the Staff Portal looks stale, check Publish Status, Historical Schedules, Regular Schedule locks, and Settings.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout"><b>Important:</b> Opening the Staff Portal shortcut does not publish schedule changes. Use the appropriate Publish action first.</div><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="publish">Publishing</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="regular">Regular Schedule</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="settings">Settings</button></div>'},
      {id:'settings',title:'Settings',nav:'settings',html:'<p>Settings controls school-specific scheduling behavior, manager display preferences, Staff Portal attendance notifications, auto-publishing, and maintenance tools. Admin access in this multi-school fork is controlled through Google-account school access in System Admin.</p><h4>Scheduling settings</h4><ul><li><b>Individual* Rescue Threshold</b> controls when high-priority uncovered students should prevent lower-priority Individual* grouping rescue logic.</li><li><b>Grouping Strategy</b> controls whether groups are built with similar priority students or mixed priority students.</li><li><b>Balance General Assignments</b> can spread general assignments across available staff instead of relying only on order/ranking.</li><li><b>Classroom Group Size Override</b> globally overrides classroom grouping limits when a positive number is entered.</li><li><b>Break/Lunch Group Size Override</b> globally overrides break/lunch grouping limits when a positive number is entered. Blank or 0 means no global override; use Student Manager Max Group Size = 0 to prevent a specific student from being temporarily grouped for rest coverage.</li><li><b>Break/Lunch Conforms to Blocking Rules</b> decides whether student blocked-staff rules still apply during break/lunch coverage.</li><li><b>Allow Emergency Lunch Coverage</b> allows staff marked Interested in Overtime to be used when lunch coverage gaps remain.</li><li><b>Staff rest scheduling</b> schedules 30-minute lunches before 15-minute breaks and flags any unscheduled staff rest in Unassigned Assignments. It ranks legal windows from the target block outward, avoids first-90-minute windows when possible, honors staff rest preferences, and uses direct temporary grouping only when enabled. Student Max Group Size = 0 prevents that student from being temporarily grouped for rest coverage.</li></ul><h4>Display and manager settings</h4><ul><li><b>Show Badges</b> controls whether issue and status badges appear by default in managers and schedule editors.</li><li>Badges are informational. Hiding badges does not remove the underlying scheduling rule or warning.</li></ul><h4>Attendance and Staff Portal settings</h4><ul><li><b>Absence notification email(s)</b> sends an email when a staff absence report is submitted through the Staff Portal.</li><li>Use commas, semicolons, spaces, or line breaks to separate multiple email addresses.</li><li><b>Auto-publish schedule</b> can publish the current working schedule before the campus workday starts.</li><li>Auto-publish uses the current working schedule. Review schedule readiness before relying on it.</li></ul><h4>Data updates and validation lists</h4><ul><li><b>Update Data Points</b> refreshes source data points and records the last refresh time.</li><li><b>Refresh Lists</b> rebuilds dropdowns, helper lists, and validation lists used by the portal.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout"><b>What this does:</b> Settings changes behavior for the currently selected school. <b>What this does not do:</b> Settings does not directly edit staff profiles, student schedules, historical snapshots, or the Staff Portal published schedule until the relevant save, generate, or publish action is run.</div><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="start">Start Here</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="staffportal">Staff Portal</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="generate">Generate</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="attendance">Attendance</button></div>'},
      {id:'logic',title:'Scheduling Logic Overview',nav:'logic',html:'<p>The scheduler balances student support needs, staff availability, attendance, bell schedule periods, classroom/location rules, off-campus site/buffer rules, structured-room limits, group capacity, individual support priority, staff priority order, and break/lunch feasibility.</p><h4>General priorities</h4><ol><li>Respect absences and blocked times.</li><li>Cover required individual support first.</li><li>Group compatible students where rules allow.</li><li>Prefer same-location coverage.</li><li>Preserve legal/required breaks and lunches where possible.</li><li>Flag unresolved conflicts rather than hiding them.</li></ol><p>Logic Review includes the Assignment Analyzer, Rule Conflict Detector, warnings, workload balance, generation summaries, and drilldown guidance. Use Assignment Analyzer when you want a staff-by-staff reason for a specific student/period. Use Rule Conflict Detector to check setup conflicts before reviewing individual rows.</p><h4>Newer rule layers</h4><ul><li><b>Special Events</b> override normal student schedule needs during the event window and protect assigned event staff from break/lunch use during that window.</li><li><b>Off-Campus Sites</b> add buffer windows and same-site/same-group coverage rules.</li><li><b>Dynamic periods</b> add/rename schedule blocks while preserving internal keys.</li><li><b>Secondary-as-Primary</b> swaps preference order on selected weekdays.</li></ul><h4>Assignment Analyzer</h4><ul><li>Use Assignment Analyzer when one student/period needs a staff-by-staff explanation.</li><li>It groups staff into Assigned, Eligible, Rejected, and Other when available.</li><li>For off-campus needs, it shows the site, site group, and buffer information.</li></ul><h4>Rule Conflict Detector</h4><ul><li>Use Rule Conflict Detector before generation or when a schedule has many warnings.</li><li>Critical items usually block generation or leave students unassigned.</li><li>Warnings and Info items explain setup risks, including off-campus coverage windows and custom period setup.</li></ul><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="generate">Generate</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="staffManager">Staff Manager</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="studentManager">Student Manager</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="faq">FAQ</button></div>'},
      {id:'faq',title:'FAQ',nav:'help',html:'<h4>Why do staff not see my changes?</h4><p>Most admin edits remain internal until the appropriate publish action runs. Check the publish status, confirm you published the intended schedule type, and ask staff to refresh the Staff Portal.</p><h4>Why is a student unassigned?</h4><p>Check whether the student has a required support/location for that period, whether the student is absent, whether all eligible staff are absent or blocked, whether blocked-student or blocked-room rules apply, and whether grouping/capacity rules prevent assignment.</p><h4>Why was a staff member not assigned?</h4><p>Review Absent Today, staff status, blocked times, blocked rooms, blocked students, priority holds, Coach hold, workload, break/lunch placement, and whether another staff member had a stronger match for the student/location.</p><h4>Why are breaks or lunches missing?</h4><p>Breaks and lunches require enough available coverage and the staff member must meet partial-day eligibility thresholds. Check staff absences, blocked times, Coach priority holds, rest preferences marked Require this time, minimum staffing, required student coverage, and whether enough feasible windows remain.</p><h4>Why does Regular Schedule not appear in the Staff Portal?</h4><p>At least one Historical Schedule must be locked as a regular schedule and Regular Schedule display must be enabled for the Staff Portal.</p><h4>What is the difference between Save Schedule and Publish Scenario?</h4><p>Save stores a scenario snapshot in Historical Schedules. Publish makes the scenario the active staff-facing schedule or upcoming schedule, depending on the workflow used.</p><h4>Can I override warnings?</h4><p>Customize Schedule warnings are usually advisory. They are meant to draw attention to risk before saving or publishing, not to replace administrator review.</p><h4>How do I get to the Staff Portal?</h4><p>Use the gray <b>Staff Portal</b> shortcut in the lower menu after configuring the Staff Portal base URL in System Admin.</p><h4>How do Special Events affect schedules?</h4><p>Saved Special Events for the active date replace normal student needs during the event window. If a staff member is assigned to the event, that staff member is protected from break/lunch coverage during the event window.</p><ul><li><b>No assigned staff</b> means the student is away from regular campus support without assigning another staff member to that event.</li><li>Blank event start uses the start of the schedule day; blank end uses the end of the schedule day.</li><li>Deleting a Special Event removes its calendar note when possible.</li></ul><h4>How do rest preferences affect break/lunch?</h4><p>Staff Manager rest preferences rank legal windows after hard rules. Prefer this time may fall back to another legal window. Require this time does not fall back; if the selected timing cannot work legally, the rest item may be left unscheduled for review.</p><h4>How do off-campus sites affect break/lunch?</h4><p>Off-campus assignments block main-campus break/lunch coverage during the assignment window plus the saved buffer. Staff at the same off-campus site or group may cover each other when support rules allow.</p><ul><li><b>Site Name</b> is the location shown in schedule selectors.</li><li><b>Site Group</b> lets related off-campus sites share coverage when support and capacity rules allow.</li><li><b>Buffer Minutes</b> protects travel/setup time before and after the off-campus assignment.</li></ul><h4>How does Secondary-as-Primary work?</h4><p>In Student Manager, select the weekday(s) when the student secondary staff should be treated as the primary preference. The base Primary/Secondary fields remain visible, but generation swaps the order on the selected days.</p><h4>What do Attendance Manager letters mean?</h4><p>Monthly Attendance uses reason codes for full-day absences: PN = Personal Necessity, I = Illness, V = Vacation, B = Bereavement, J = Jury Duty, and P = Personal Reason. Partial-day entries may show the code plus missed hours.</p><h4>Why did a renamed period not show somewhere?</h4><p>Refresh Data after saving Bell Schedule period setup. Current screens should use display labels, while old historical snapshots may preserve the label that existed when the snapshot was saved.</p><h4>What should I do first when something looks wrong?</h4><ol><li>Refresh Data.</li><li>Check Dashboard status tiles.</li><li>Open Logic Review.</li><li>Use Logic Drilldown on the relevant row.</li><li>Review the relevant Staff Manager or Student Manager rule.</li><li>Republish if the Staff Portal is stale.</li></ol><div class="helpCallout"><b>Related topics:</b> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="start">Start Here</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="logic">Scheduling Logic</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="settings">Settings</button> <button class="btn small" data-help-target="staffportal">Staff Portal</button></div>'}
    ];
}


