er="Optional setup notes"></textarea><div class="toolbar"><button id="mcCreateBtn" class="btn primary" data-action="multi-campus-create">Create School</button><button id="mcCancelEditBtn" class="btn" data-action="multi-campus-cancel-edit" style="display:none">Cancel Edit</button><button class="btn" data-action="multi-campus-load">Reload</button></div></div></div><div class="mcSystemColV5302 mcSystemRightV5302"><div class="card wideCard mcAccessCardV5301"><h2>Assign User Access <span class="helpDot" tabindex="0" data-tip="District users have access to all schools. Site users can be assigned to one or more schools. Active access allows login/use. Inactive keeps the row for a temporary hold or audit note. The trash icon removes the access row from the registry; it does not delete the Google account.">?</span></h2><input id="mcUserOriginalEmail" type="hidden"><input id="mcUserOriginalRole" type="hidden"><div class="accessGrid"><div><label>Email</label><input id="mcUserEmail" placeholder="user@domain.org"></div><div><label>Role</label><select id="mcUserRole"><option>Site</option><option>District</option></select></div><div id="mcUserCampusWrap" class="campusAccessField"><select id="mcUserCampus" class="campusAccessSelector" multiple aria-label="Choose schools"></select><div id="mcCampusPicker" class="campusPicker"><button type="button" class="btn campusPickerBtn" data-action="campus-picker-toggle">Choose schools</button><div id="mcCampusChips" class="campusChips">No schools selected</div><div id="mcCampusPanel" class="campusPickerPanel"></div></div></div><div><label>Status</label><select id="mcUserStatus"><option>Active</option><option>Inactive</option></select></div><button id="mcUserSaveBtn" class="btn primary" data-action="multi-campus-add-user">Save Access</button><button id="mcUserCancelEditBtn" class="btn" data-action="multi-campus-cancel-user-edit" style="display:none">Cancel</button></div><div class="userEditNote" id="mcUserEditNote"></div><div id="mcUserList" class="compactList" style="margin-top:12px"></div></div><div class="card wideCard" id="performanceToolsCardV5397" style="margin-top:12px">  <h2>Cache Warming &amp; Sheet Health <span class="helpDot" tabindex="0" data-tip="Pre-warms selected-school caches and audits/cleans excess blank rows/columns. Manual tools run only when clicked. Automatic warming runs before the school day based on the selected bell schedule.">?</span></h2>  <p class="muted">Use these tools to warm school-specific caches and check whether sheets have inflated blank rows/columns that can slow loading.</p>  <div class="toolbar" style="margin-top:8px;flex-wrap:wrap"><button class="btn primary" type="button" data-action="perf-warm-selected-v5397">Warm Selected School</button><button class="btn" type="button" data-action="perf-warm-all-v5397">Warm All Schools</button><button class="btn" type="button" data-action="perf-audit-sheets-v5397">Audit Selected School Sheets</button><button class="btn" type="button" data-action="perf-clean-sheets-v5397">Clean Selected School Sheets</button></div>  <div class="inline" style="align-items:end;margin-top:10px"><label class="tinyCheck"><input id="autoWarmEnabledV5397" type="checkbox" style="width:auto"> Automatically warm before school</label><div><label>Minutes before school</label><select id="autoWarmMinutesV5397"><option>60</option><option>45</option><option selected>30</option><option>15</option></select></div><button class="btn" type="button" data-action="perf-auto-save-v5397">Save Auto Warm</button></div>  <div id="performanceToolsStatusV5397" class="muted" style="margin-top:8px">Ready.</div></div></div></div><div id="systemAdminVersionV5307" class="systemAdminVersionV5306" style="position:absolute;right:12px;bottom:6px;font-size:11px;line-height:1.2;color:#6b7280;font-weight:500;pointer-events:none;">${getHardCodedSystemAdminVersionTextV5361_()}</div></section>

  <section id="settings" class="section"><div class="card"><h2>Settings</h2><div class="grid three"><div><label>Individual* Rescue Threshold</label><div class="muted">Students who are not covered and who have a priority ranking above this number will not trigger Individual* students being grouped.</div><input id="setIndividualStarThreshold" type="number"></div><div><label>Grouping Strategy</label><div class="muted">Heterogeneous = groups mix high- and low-priority students.<br>Homogeneous = groups students with similar priority together.</div><select id="setGroupingStrategy"><option>Homogeneous</option><option>Heterogeneous</option></select></div><div><label>Balance General Assignments</label><div class="muted">Yes = when two or more staff are available, prefer staff with fewer current assignments.<br>No = assign based off availability and order/ranking.</div><select id="setBalanceGeneral"><option>Yes</option><option>No</option></select></div><div><label>Show Badges</label><div class="muted">Yes = show issue/status badges in the managers and schedule editor.<br>No = hide badges by default.</div><select id="setShowBadges"><option>Yes</option><option>No</option></select></div><div><label>Classroom Group Size Override</label><div class="muted">Blank or 0 = no global override. Any positive value overrides student-specific grouping limits during Periods 1–6 and Break.</div><input id="setClassroomGroupSize" type="number"></div><div><label>Break/Lunch Group Size Override</label><div class="muted">Blank or 0 = no global override. Any positive value overrides student-specific grouping limits during break/lunch coverage. To prevent grouping for a specific student during break/lunch coverage, set that student's Max Group Size to 0 in Student Manager.</div><input id="setLunchGroupSize" type="number"></div><div><label>Break/Lunch Conforms to Blocking Rules</label><div class="muted">Yes = for break/lunch coverage, students remain blocked from specific staff as indicated.<br>No = for break/lunch coverage, students are NOT blocked and can be supported by any staff.</div><select id="setLunchBlocking"><option>Yes</option><option>No</option></select></div><div><label>Allow Emergency Lunch Coverage</label><div class="muted">Yes = when students remain uncovered after the normal schedule and break process, staff marked as being interested in overtime will be scheduled without a lunch break.<br>No = staff overtime interest will not be used as a potential option to improve scheduling shortfalls.</div><select id="setEmergencyLunch"><option>Yes</option><option>No</option></select></div><div><label>Temporarily Group to Ensure Staff Breaks/Lunch</label><div class="muted">Yes = if a staff break/lunch cannot be covered by a truly free staff member, allow direct same-location temporary grouping for that rest window only. If direct grouping cannot solve the rest need, protected Lead coverage may be used, and daisy-chain is only considered as a final pass after all non-daisy options fail. Options are scored to avoid disrupting lower numeric priority students whenever possible.</div><select id="setTemporaryGroupForRest"><option>No</option><option>Yes</option></select></div><div><label>Allow Behavior Interventionist → Instruction</label><div class="muted">Yes = Behavior Interventionists may be used as fallback for Instruction support and for break/lunch coverage of Instruction needs. Exact Behavior matches are still prioritized first.</div><select id="setAllowBIToInstruction"><option>No</option><option>Yes</option></select></div><div><label>Allow Special Education Assistant → Behavior</label><div class="muted">Yes = Special Education Assistants may be used as fallback for Behavior support and for break/lunch coverage of Behavior needs. Exact Behavior Interventionist matches are still prioritized first.</div><select id="setAllowSEAToBehavior"><option>No</option><option>Yes</option></select></div><div><label>Alert Rules</label><div class="muted">Controls which newer schedule choke points are flagged in managers and Logic Review.</div><div class="settingsMiniChecks"><label><input type="checkbox" id="setAlertRestPrefs"> Rest preference alerts</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="setAlertRequiredRestOnly"> Required rest alerts only</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="setAlertSupportMismatch"> Support-type mismatch alerts</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="setAlertSupportCapacity"> Support-type capacity alerts</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="setAlertPartialDayRest"> Partial-day rest eligibility alerts</label></div></div><div><label>Absence notification email(s)</label><div class="muted">Enter one or more email addresses. Separate with commas, semicolons, spaces, or line breaks. These addresses are notified when a staff absence report is submitted.</div><textarea id="setAbsenceNotifyEmails" placeholder="name@example.edu"></textarea></div><div><label>Auto-publish schedule</label><div class="muted">Optional. Automatically publishes the current working schedule before the workday starts.</div><select id="setAutoPublishOffset"><option value="">None</option><option value="15">15 minutes before start</option><option value="30">30 minutes before start</option><option value="45">45 minutes before start</option><option value="60">60 minutes before start</option></select></div><div><label>Auto-clear last published schedule</label><div class="muted">Optional. Clears the current staff-facing published schedule after the school day ends.</div><select id="setAutoClearPublishedOffset"><option value="">None</option><option value="30">30 minutes after school</option><option value="60">1 hour after school</option><option value="120">2 hours after school</option><option value="180">3 hours after school</option></select></div><div><label>Clear current published schedule</label><div class="muted">Immediately removes the current staff-facing published schedule. Historical snapshots remain saved.</div><button class="btn" data-action="settings-clear-published">Clear Published Schedule</button></div><div><label>Data Updates</label><div class="muted" id="folderLastRefresh">Last refreshed on: Not recorded</div><button class="btn" data-run="folders">Update Data Points</button></div><div><label>Validation Lists</label><div class="muted">Rebuilds dropdowns and helper lists.</div><button class="btn" data-run="setup">Refresh Lists</button></div><div id="dataHealthToolsV5340"><label>Data Health Check <span class="helpDot" tabindex="0" data-tip="Checks for common database problems, validates current/active staff counts, and can remove spreadsheet validation rules because edits are handled through the Admin Portal UI.">?</span></label><div class="muted">Run a quick database check. Use Stabilize Database once to clear sheet validation rules and add missing stable IDs for staff/students.</div><div class="toolbar"><button class="btn" data-action="data-health-check">Run Health Check</button><button class="btn primary" data-action="database-stabilize">Stabilize Database</button></div><div id="dataHealthResultV5340" class="muted" style="margin-top:6px"></div></div><div id="staffQrLetterToolsV5317"><label>Staff QR letters <span class="helpDot" tabindex="0" data-tip="Edit the staff letter template and generate a print-ready PDF for the currently selected school. Each active staff member gets one page with their unique Staff Portal QR code and cut-out card.">?</span></label><div class="muted">Generate one letter per active staff member for this school with their unique Staff Portal QR code.</div><button class="btn" data-action="staff-qr-letter-open">Edit Letter Template & Generate Staff Letters</button></div><div id="directDatabaseToolsV5322" class="directDbToolsInlineV5326"><label>Directly Edit Database <span class="helpDot" tabindex="0" data-tip="Warning: direct spreadsheet edits bypass portal validation and can break scheduling data. Only use this for careful maintenance or emergency repair.">?</span></label><div class="muted">Open the underlying database spreadsheet for direct edits. Use carefully; changes here bypass portal validation.</div><button class="btn danger directDbBtnV5322" id="directDatabaseLinkV5332" data-action="direct-db-open" data-direct-database-link type="button" title="Open the selected school database spreadsheet. Warning: direct spreadsheet edits bypass portal validation and can break scheduling data.">Directly Edit Database</button></div></div><div style="height:12px"></div><div class="toolbar"><button class="btn primary" data-action="settings-save">Save Settings</button><button class="btn" data-action="settings-load">Reload Settings</button></div></div></section>
